package card

const pageHTML = `<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'none'; font-src 'none'; connect-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'">
<title>{{.Title}}</title>
{{template "style" .}}</head><body>
<a class="skip" href="#findings">Skip to findings</a>
<header class="masthead"><span>ARO HCP / Field notes</span><span>Portable performance card</span></header>
<main>
<header class="hero"><div class="pills"><span>{{.Card.status}}</span><span>Measured {{.Card.measuredDate}}</span><span>{{.Card.scope.environment}}</span></div>
<h1>{{.Title}}</h1><p class="lead">Resource requests are proposed operating budgets, not a performance ceiling.</p>
<p class="scope">Characterized envelope, not a support contract. Production: {{text .Card.scope.production}}. Capacity qualification: {{text .Card.scope.capacityQualification}}.</p></header>
{{template "budget" .}}
<nav aria-label="Report sections"><a href="#budget">Proposed budget</a><a href="#findings">Findings</a><a href="#experience">Client experience</a><a href="#component-usage">Resources</a><a href="#method">Method</a><a href="#contention">Contention</a><a href="#clientload">Client load</a><a href="#evidence">Evidence</a></nav>
<section id="findings"><div class="section-heading"><span class="index">01 / Findings</span><h2>What the observations support</h2></div>
<p>{{.Lead}}</p>
<div class="findings">
<article><span class="eyebrow">Population screen</span><h3>{{n .Card.population.applicationPodsReady 0}} <small>Pods</small></h3><p>{{n .Card.population.deployments 0}} applications, {{n .Card.population.replicasPerDeployment 0}} Pods each. {{n .Card.densityScreens.scoringSeconds 0}}-second scoring screens, not a soak or an API-throughput qualification.</p><a href="#density">See every density step</a></article>
<article><span class="eyebrow">Client body completion</span><h3>{{n .FirstArm.successfulQPSActiveDenominatorIncludingDrainCompletions 2}} <small>QPS</small></h3><p>At {{n .Card.apfComparison.client.offeredQPS 0}} offered QPS and {{n .FirstArm.shares 0}} APF shares, over a {{n .Card.apfComparison.client.durationSecondsPerArm 0}}-second arm. Active-time denominator includes drain completions.</p><a href="#clientload">Shedding and latency, together</a></article>
<article><span class="eyebrow">Observed safety, not full grace</span><h3>{{if .NoObservedCrash}}No observed OOM / restart{{else}}Safety evidence{{end}}</h3><p>{{n .Card.health.safety.observations 0}} safety observations; {{n .Card.health.safety.recordedNewOOM 0}} recorded new OOMs; {{n .Card.health.safety.restartDeltas 0}} restart deltas. {{n .Card.health.workload.boundedRolloutFailures 0}} bounded rollout failure(s). Successful LIST p95: {{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}{{n .successfulLISTP95Seconds 2}}s ({{n .shares 0}} shares); {{end}}safety and responsiveness are separate observations.</p><a href="#evidence">Read the observation limits</a></article>
</div><p class="annotation">{{.Card.apfComparison.achievedBehavior}}</p></section>
{{template "experience" .}}
{{template "resource-usage" .}}
<section id="method"><div class="section-heading"><span class="index">02 / Method</span><h2>Separate the population, pressure and observers</h2></div>
<div class="lanes" aria-label="Experiment topology">
<article><h3>Management hosts</h3><strong>{{n .Card.topology.managementHosts.count 0}} x {{.Card.topology.managementHosts.sku}}</strong><p>{{n .Card.topology.managementHosts.rawCPUCoresEach 0}} cores / {{n .Card.topology.managementHosts.rawMemoryGiBEach 0}} GiB each</p><p>{{n .Card.resourceProfile.kas.replicas 0}} kube-apiservers + {{n .Card.resourceProfile.etcd.replicas 0}} etcd replicas<br>HCP services + runnable CPU competitors</p></article>
<article><h3>Guest workers</h3><strong>{{n .Card.topology.guestWorkers.count 0}} x {{.Card.topology.guestWorkers.sku}}</strong><p>{{n .Card.population.deployments 0}} applications x {{n .Card.population.replicasPerDeployment 0}} Pods</p><p>{{n .Card.population.totalActiveGuestPods 0}} total active Pods, including {{n .Card.population.otherActiveGuestPods 0}} platform Pods. {{n .Card.population.aggregateFreePodSlotsBeforeSurgeCanary 0}} aggregate slots before surge/canary.</p></article>
<article><h3>Observer placement methodology</h3><strong>Keep measurement off the contended worker pool</strong><p>Observers should run on infra; node exporters on measured workers. This is placement guidance, not a claim verified by the card metadata. Measurement overhead still needs accounting.</p></article></div>
<ol class="pipeline" aria-label="Run sequence"><li>Seed population</li><li>Warm-up + baseline</li><li>CPU competition</li><li>{{n .Card.apfComparison.client.durationSecondsPerArm 0}}s client arms</li><li>{{n .Card.apfComparison.background.recoverySeconds 0}}s recovery</li></ol>
<p>{{.Card.apfComparison.design}}. {{.Card.scope.history}}</p>
<details><summary>Canary: a small scale-up and cleanup, not just an API ping</summary><p>A protected Deployment goes 0 -&gt; 1 -&gt; 0. ACK measures the scale-write acknowledgement. Ready starts at the same scale-up intent and includes ACK; do not add the two. Cleanup includes watch setup. Watches avoid a polling-floor latency.</p><p>The soft 3x-baseline threshold records degradation; it is not an abort. Hard ACK / Ready / Cleanup deadlines are {{n .Card.apfComparison.protectedCanaries.hardACKSeconds 0}} / {{n .Card.apfComparison.protectedCanaries.hardReadySeconds 0}} / {{n .Card.apfComparison.protectedCanaries.hardCleanupSeconds 0}} seconds.</p></details>
<h3 id="density">Population screens: a separate {{n .Card.densityScreens.scoringSeconds 0}}-second window per step</h3>
<figure><div id="density-chart" class="chart"></div><figcaption>Application Pod count, not API QPS. Dots mark the population of each reported scoring case; completion outcomes remain in the table.</figcaption></figure>
<div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Density outcomes; recovery {{n .Card.densityScreens.recoverySeconds 0}} seconds</caption><thead><tr><th>Application Pods</th><th>Rollouts complete / scheduled</th><th>Canaries complete / expected</th><th>Soft degraded</th><th>Capture</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{range .Card.densityScreens.cases}}<tr><th>{{n .applicationPods 0}}</th><td>{{n .completedRollouts 0}} / {{n .scheduledRollouts 0}}</td><td>{{n .completedCanaries 0}} / {{n $.Card.densityScreens.steadyCanariesEach 0}}</td><td>{{n .softDegradedCanaries 0}}</td><td>{{text $.Card.densityScreens.captureStatusAllCases}}</td></tr>{{end}}</tbody></table></div>
<p>Replacement schedule: one per application per {{n .Card.densityScreens.replacementPeriodPerAppSeconds 0}} seconds; max outstanding {{n .Card.densityScreens.maxOutstanding 0}}. This schedule is not an hour-long soak. No manual QPS coverage or breaking point is inferred.</p><ul>{{range .Card.densityScreens.limitations}}<li>{{.}}</li>{{end}}</ul>
</section>
<section id="contention"><div class="section-heading"><span class="index">03 / Contention</span><h2>CPU adversaries are a test condition</h2></div>
<p>Competitors fill {{n .Card.apfComparison.cpuCompetition.fillPercentOfFreeRequestedHeadroom 0}}% of free <em>requested</em> CPU headroom, not a utilization target. Frozen requests: {{range .Card.apfComparison.cpuCompetition.frozenRequestsMilli}}{{n . 0}}m; {{end}}{{n .Card.apfComparison.cpuCompetition.burnWorkersEach 0}} burn workers each. Unchanged between arms: {{text .Card.apfComparison.cpuCompetition.unchangedBetweenArms}}.</p>
<aside class="annotation">{{if .Contention}}Short pre-start reference, not a controlled idle-cluster experiment. {{end}}Where observed, a high node-utilization plateau supports the contention condition, not a causal estimate of its effect. Competitor requests alone do not establish continuous CPU consumption.</aside>
{{if .Contention}}<p class="muted">Swipe horizontally on narrow screens; use worker toggles to isolate traces.</p><div id="contention-charts"></div><p class="muted">CPU busy and burner CPU use separate axes. UTC is shared; nulls break lines, and missing samples are never zero-filled. Coverage strips remain visible when traces are hidden. No sample (not zero) also applies before burner startup; it does not necessarily mean lost capture. CPU rates trail {{n .Contention.method.cpuRateWindowSeconds 0}} seconds. Busy includes iowait and steal, not just useful work.</p>
<div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>CPU PSI: waiting wall-time fraction, not percent CPU utilization; finite-sample medians only</caption><thead><tr><th>Window</th><th>Worker</th><th>CPU busy median % (valid / expected)</th><th>Burner median cores</th><th>PSI stall median % (valid / expected)</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{range .Contention.summary}}{{if ne .id "timeline"}}{{$window := .id}}{{range .nodes}}<tr><th>{{$window}}</th><td>{{.id}}</td><td>{{n .busyPercent.median 3}} ({{n .busyPercent.sampleCount 0}} / {{n .busyPercent.expectedSampleCount 0}})</td><td>{{n .adversaryCores.median 3}}</td><td>{{n .psiPercent.median 3}} ({{n .psiPercent.sampleCount 0}} / {{n .psiPercent.expectedSampleCount 0}})</td></tr>{{end}}{{end}}{{end}}</tbody></table></div>
<p class="muted">Coverage counts evaluation slots, not independent scrapes or duration coverage. A null PSI median is unknown, never zero.</p><ul>{{range .Contention.limitations}}<li>{{.}}</li>{{end}}</ul><details><summary>Contention source labels, coverage and SHA-256</summary><pre>{{pretty .Contention}}</pre></details>{{else}}<p class="empty">No node time series supplied. No raw artifacts were opened.</p>{{end}}
</section>
<section id="clientload"><div class="section-heading"><span class="index">04 / Client load</span><h2>Throughput, shedding and responsiveness</h2></div>
<p>{{n .Card.apfComparison.client.identities 0}} identities; {{n .Card.apfComparison.client.offeredQPS 0}} offered QPS per arm, {{n .Card.apfComparison.client.durationSecondsPerArm 0}} seconds; max in flight {{n .Card.apfComparison.client.maxInFlight 0}}; request/body timeout {{n .Card.apfComparison.client.requestTimeoutSeconds 0}} seconds.</p>
<div class="chart-pair"><figure><h3>Offered vs body-complete throughput</h3><div id="throughput-chart" class="chart"></div><figcaption>QPS. Successful bodies including drain completions / actual active scheduling span. Outlined bars show offered rate on the same axis.</figcaption></figure><figure><h3>Successful-request p95</h3><div id="latency-chart" class="chart"></div><figcaption>Seconds, GET and LIST on the same axis. Success-only latency excludes rejected and timed-out requests.</figcaption></figure></div>
<figure><h3>What happened to the offers?</h3><div id="outcomes-chart" class="chart"></div><figcaption>Counts use logical offers as denominator, not HTTP attempts. A stack requires a positive offer count, an exact sum of the four reported counts, and matching experience evidence explicitly recording zero HTTP 429/timeout overlap and zero other errors. An equal sum alone does not prove a disjoint partition; otherwise see the table. HTTP 200 with body timeout is not a success.</figcaption></figure>
<div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Per-arm counts and explicit denominators</caption><thead><tr><th>Metric</th>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<th>{{n .shares 0}} shares</th>{{end}}</tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th>Start UTC</th>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<td>{{utc .startEpoch}}</td>{{end}}</tr><tr><th>Stop UTC</th>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<td>{{utc .stopEpoch}}</td>{{end}}</tr>
<tr><th>Offers (stack denominator)</th>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<td>{{n .offered 0}}</td>{{end}}</tr><tr><th>Dispatched logical requests</th>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<td>{{n .dispatched 0}}</td>{{end}}</tr><tr><th>HTTP attempts (separate count)</th>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<td>{{n .httpAttempts 0}}</td>{{end}}</tr>
<tr><th>Successful bodies</th>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<td>{{n .successfulBodies 0}}</td>{{end}}</tr><tr><th>HTTP 429</th>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<td>{{n .http429 0}}</td>{{end}}</tr><tr><th>Body/request timeouts</th>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<td>{{n .timeouts 0}}</td>{{end}}</tr><tr><th>HTTP 200 with body timeout (subset)</th>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<td>{{n .http200WithBodyTimeout 0}}</td>{{end}}</tr><tr><th>Generator-limited offers</th>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<td>{{n .generatorLimited 0}}</td>{{end}}</tr>
<tr><th>Body-complete QPS / active time</th>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<td>{{n .successfulQPSActiveDenominatorIncludingDrainCompletions 3}}</td>{{end}}</tr><tr><th>Body-complete QPS / wall time including drain</th>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<td>{{n .successfulQPSWallIncludingDrain 3}}</td>{{end}}</tr><tr><th>Bodies completed strictly within active window</th>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<td>{{n .successfulCompletedWithinActive 0}}</td>{{end}}</tr>
<tr><th>Successful GET / LIST p95 (s)</th>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<td>{{n .successfulGETP95Seconds 3}} / {{n .successfulLISTP95Seconds 3}}</td>{{end}}</tr>
<tr><th>Hard-completed canaries / expected</th>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<td>{{n .hardCompletedCanaries 0}} / {{n $.Card.apfComparison.protectedCanaries.perArm 0}}</td>{{end}}</tr><tr><th>Soft-degraded canaries</th>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<td>{{n .softDegradedCanaries 0}}</td>{{end}}</tr><tr><th>Bounded completed / accepted background rollouts</th>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<td>{{n .boundedCompletedRollouts 0}} / {{n .acceptedRollouts 0}}</td>{{end}}</tr><tr><th>Eventually converged rollouts, when reported</th>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<td>{{n .eventuallyConvergedRollouts 0}}</td>{{end}}</tr>
<tr><th>Nominal seats per KAS</th>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<td>{{n .nominalSeatsEach 0}}</td>{{end}}</tr><tr><th>Sampled current seats range</th>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<td>{{range .sampledCurrentSeatsRange}}{{n . 0}} {{else}}unknown{{end}}</td>{{end}}</tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p class="annotation">A late-converged rollout remains a bounded failure, not a rejected write or an observed crash. {{if .LimitedArms}}Generator-limited offers were recorded at {{range .LimitedArms}}{{n .shares 0}} shares ({{n .generatorLimited 0}} offers); {{end}}achieved throughput is a biased plateau, not true APF capacity. {{end}}{{.Card.apfComparison.apf.interpretation}}</p>
<details><summary>Client mix, transport, background schedule and APF settings</summary><p>{{.Card.apfComparison.client.transport}}</p><pre>{{pretty .Card.apfComparison.client}}</pre><pre>{{pretty .Card.apfComparison.background}}</pre><pre>{{pretty .Card.apfComparison.apf}}</pre></details></section>
<section id="resources"><div class="section-heading"><span class="index">05 / Resources</span><h2>Requests are not usage, and soft is not hard</h2></div>
<p>Profile <code>{{.Card.resourceProfile.profile}}</code>. {{.Card.resourceProfile.resolution}}</p>
<div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Per-container policy, not a whole-HCP hard cap</caption><thead><tr><th>Container</th><th>CPU request (m)</th><th>Memory request (MiB)</th><th>Hard memory (MiB)</th><th>Go soft target (MiB)</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th>Kube-apiserver (each of {{n .Card.resourceProfile.kas.replicas 0}})</th><td>{{n .Card.resourceProfile.kas.cpuMilli 0}}</td><td>{{n .Card.resourceProfile.kas.memoryMiB 0}}</td><td>{{n .Card.resourceProfile.kas.hardMemoryMiB 0}}</td><td>{{n (div .Card.resourceProfile.kas.goSoftTargetBytes 1048576) 1}}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Etcd (each of {{n .Card.resourceProfile.etcd.replicas 0}})</th><td>{{n .Card.resourceProfile.etcd.cpuMilli 0}}</td><td>{{n .Card.resourceProfile.etcd.memoryMiB 0}}</td><td>{{n .Card.resourceProfile.etcd.hardMemoryMiB 0}}</td><td>{{n (div .Card.resourceProfile.etcd.goSoftTargetBytes 1048576) 1}}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Catalog ({{n .Card.resourceProfile.catalog.deployedRegistries 0}} deployed registries)</th><td>{{n .Card.resourceProfile.catalog.cpuMilli 0}}</td><td>{{n .Card.resourceProfile.catalog.memoryMiB 0}}</td><td>{{n .Card.resourceProfile.catalog.hardMemoryMiB 0}}</td><td>{{n (div .Card.resourceProfile.catalog.goSoftTargetBytes 1048576) 1}}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Policy fallback (derived)</th><td>{{n .Card.resourceProfile.policyDefaultRequests.cpuMilli 0}}</td><td>{{n .Card.resourceProfile.policyDefaultRequests.memoryMiB 0}}</td><td>{{n (mul .Card.resourceProfile.policyDefaultRequests.memoryMiB .Card.resourceProfile.memorySafetyMultiplier) 0}}</td><td>{{n (div (mul .Card.resourceProfile.policyDefaultRequests.memoryMiB .Card.resourceProfile.goMemoryPercentOfRequest) 100) 1}}</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div><p>{{.Card.resourceProfile.coverageCaveat}} The remaining {{n .Card.resourceProfile.overrideCount 0}}-override profile is identified below, not reconstructed from Markdown. Non-Go exceptions: {{range .Card.resourceProfile.nonGoExceptions}}<code>{{.}}</code> {{end}}</p>
<div class="resource-notes"><article><h3>Whole-HCP running requests</h3><p class="stat">{{n .Card.topology.requestAccounting.includingExperimentalKSM.memoryGiB 3}} GiB <span>/ {{n (div .Card.topology.requestAccounting.includingExperimentalKSM.cpuMilli 1000) 2}} CPU</span></p><p>Comparison inventory, including experimental KSM. {{.Card.topology.requestAccounting.method}}</p><p>{{.Card.topology.requestAccounting.auditState}}</p></article>
<article><h3>Earlier whole-HCP sampled usage</h3><p class="stat">{{n .Card.resourceUse.earlierDirectLoadEstimate.maxSummedCgroupUsageGiB 3}} GiB</p><p>{{.Card.resourceUse.earlierDirectLoadEstimate.case}}<br>{{.Card.resourceUse.earlierDirectLoadEstimate.caseWindowStart}} to {{.Card.resourceUse.earlierDirectLoadEstimate.caseWindowEnd}}</p><p>Max simultaneous summed cgroup usage, not the later APF comparison. CPU maximum {{n .Card.resourceUse.earlierDirectLoadEstimate.maxSummedCPUCores 3}} cores occurred separately.</p></article></div>
{{if and .Shares100Arm .Card.resourceUse.comparison.shares100BusiestKAS}}<h3>Latest comparison: busiest KAS, not whole HCP</h3>{{if knownNumber .Card.resourceUse.comparison.shares100BusiestKAS.cgroupUsageMaxMiB}}<p>100-share active window: cgroup usage sampled maximum <strong>{{n .Card.resourceUse.comparison.shares100BusiestKAS.cgroupUsageMaxMiB 3}} MiB</strong>, against {{n .Card.resourceProfile.kas.memoryMiB 0}} MiB request and {{n .Card.resourceProfile.kas.hardMemoryMiB 0}} MiB hard limit. Cgroup usage is not RSS.</p>{{end}}{{if knownNumber .Card.resourceUse.comparison.shares100BusiestKAS.goManagedMaxMiBRounded}}<p>Separately in the 100-share active window, Go-managed sampled maximum <strong>{{n .Card.resourceUse.comparison.shares100BusiestKAS.goManagedMaxMiBRounded 3}} MiB</strong> against the {{n (div .Card.resourceProfile.kas.goSoftTargetBytes 1048576) 1}} MiB soft target. Go-managed memory is not RSS.</p>{{end}}{{end}}<p>{{.Card.resourceUse.comparison.wholeHCPUsageReason}}</p>{{if .Card.resourceUse.interpretation}}<p><strong>API-window interpretation; partial source coverage:</strong> {{.Card.resourceUse.interpretation}}</p>{{end}}
{{if .Card.cost}}<details open><summary>Illustrative raw allocation cost, not a bill</summary><p>Target {{.Card.cost.currency}} {{n .Card.cost.targetPerHCPHour 3}} / HCP-hour. {{.Card.cost.priceScope}}</p><code>{{.Card.cost.formula}}</code><div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Divisible raw CPU/memory lower bound; separate demand bases</caption><thead><tr><th>Basis</th><th>D16s_v6 USD/HCP-hour</th><th>E16s_v6 USD/HCP-hour</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{range .Card.cost.illustrationsRoundedUSDPerHCPHour}}<tr><th>{{.basis}}</th><td>{{n .D16s_v6 6}}</td><td>{{n .E16s_v6 6}}</td></tr>{{end}}</tbody></table></div><p>Excluded: {{range .Card.cost.exclusions}}{{.}}; {{end}}</p><p>{{.Card.cost.limitations}}</p></details>{{end}}
<details><summary>Full profile, inventory accounting and resource-window method</summary><pre>{{pretty .Card.resourceProfile}}</pre><pre>{{pretty .Card.topology}}</pre><pre>{{pretty .Card.resourceUse}}</pre></details></section>
<section id="evidence"><div class="section-heading"><span class="index">06 / Evidence</span><h2>Completion, safety and capture are different claims</h2></div>
<div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Independent evidence dimensions</caption><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Observed result</th><th>Boundary</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th>Workload</th><td>{{n .Card.health.workload.fullAPIArmsCompleted 0}} API arms; {{n .Card.health.workload.hardCompletedCanaries 0}} hard-completed / {{n .Card.health.workload.softDegradedCanaries 0}} soft-degraded canaries</td><td>Crash point: {{text .Card.health.workload.crashPoint}}. Not a crash-threshold search result.</td></tr>
<tr><th>Safety</th><td>{{n .Card.health.safety.observations 0}} observations; {{n .Card.health.safety.recordedNewOOM 0}} new OOM; {{n .Card.health.safety.restartDeltas 0}} restart deltas</td><td>{{.Card.health.safety.scope}}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Recorder</th><td>{{n .Card.health.recordio.polls 0}} polls / {{n .Card.health.recordio.samples 0}} samples. Live incomplete: {{text .Card.health.recordio.liveIncomplete}}; shutdown: {{text .Card.health.recordio.shutdown}}</td><td>{{.Card.health.recordio.scope}}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Metrics</th><td>{{n .Card.health.metricCoverage.queryRecordsSuccessful 0}} successful / {{n .Card.health.metricCoverage.queryRecordsIncomplete 0}} incomplete query records; {{text .Card.health.metricCoverage.state}}</td><td>APF/Go maximum gaps about {{range $arm, $gap := .Card.health.metricCoverage.apfGoMaxGapSecondsApproximate}}{{$arm}}: {{n $gap 0}}s; {{end}}{{n .Card.health.metricCoverage.missingTreatmentManagementNodeCPUPSI 0}} treatment node CPU/PSI series missing.</td></tr>
<tr><th>Integrity</th><td>{{n .Card.health.integrity.reviewVerifiedRawFiles 0}} files / {{n .Card.health.integrity.reviewVerifiedBytes 0}} bytes verified; {{n .Card.health.integrity.reviewRawMismatches 0}} mismatches</td><td>{{.Card.health.integrity.scope}}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Finalization</th><td>{{text .Card.health.finalization.actualOutcome}}; all children stopped: {{text .Card.health.finalization.allChildrenStopped}}</td><td>{{.Card.health.finalization.reconciliation}}</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>{{.Card.evidencePolicy.precision}} {{.Card.evidencePolicy.privateSources}}</p>
<details><summary>Citations: source paths and file SHA-256 (labels, not network links)</summary><p>{{.Card.evidencePolicy.hashMeaning}}</p><dl class="citations">{{range .Card.citations}}<dt>{{.id}}</dt><dd><code>{{.sourceFile}}</code><br><code>SHA-256 {{.sha256}}</code>{{range .membersRead}}<br>Archive member: <code>{{.}}</code>{{end}}</dd>{{end}}</dl></details>
<details><summary>Full reviewed card JSON, including retained limitations and recommendations</summary><pre>{{pretty .Card}}</pre></details>
</section><footer>Offline report / reviewed portable inputs only / no raw evidence fetched</footer>
</main><noscript><p class="annotation">JavaScript is disabled. All headline values, inventory budgets and comparison tables remain available. Resource charts and expandable raw points require JavaScript; the complete resource data is retained in the document's report-data JSON.</p></noscript>
<script id="report-data" type="application/json">{{.JSON}}</script>{{template "script" .}}{{template "resource-script" .}}{{template "experience-script" .}}</body></html>`

const pageCSS = `{{define "style"}}<style>
:root{color-scheme:light;--paper:#f6f4ed;--ink:#1d302e;--muted:#566763;--teal:#08796f;--orange:#bc5b21;--line:#ccd4cd;--white:#fffef9}*{box-sizing:border-box}html{scroll-behavior:smooth;scroll-padding-top:2rem}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font:16px/1.65 system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",sans-serif}main,.masthead{max-width:1200px;margin:auto;padding:0 44px}.masthead{padding-top:24px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:.74rem;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)}.hero{padding:70px 0 34px;max-width:960px}h1,h2,h3,p,figure{margin:0 0 1rem}h1,h2{font-family:Georgia,"Times New Roman",serif;font-weight:400;line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-.035em}h1{font-size:clamp(2.8rem,6.2vw,5.7rem);max-width:950px;margin:24px 0}h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.1rem)}h3{font-size:1.06rem;line-height:1.35}p{max-width:92ch}.lead{font-family:Georgia,"Times New Roman",serif;font-size:clamp(1.25rem,2.4vw,1.65rem);line-height:1.5;max-width:780px}.scope,.muted,figcaption{font-size:.84rem;color:var(--muted)}.pills{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap}.pills span{padding:3px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:20px;font-size:.72rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em}.pills span:first-child{background:#e6ede6;color:#285c48}nav{display:flex;gap:25px;flex-wrap:wrap;border-block:1px solid var(--line);padding:16px 0}a{color:var(--teal);text-underline-offset:4px}nav a{text-decoration:none;font-size:.88rem;font-weight:600}a:hover{text-decoration:underline}a:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--orange);outline-offset:4px}section{padding:56px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.index,.eyebrow{display:block;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.14em;font-size:.7rem;font-weight:650;color:var(--teal);margin-bottom:14px}.section-heading{margin-bottom:28px}.findings,.lanes{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:24px}.findings article{border-top:3px solid var(--teal);padding:23px 0}.findings h3{font-family:Georgia,"Times New Roman",serif;font-size:2rem;font-weight:400;line-height:1.15}.findings h3 small{font:1rem system-ui,sans-serif}.findings p,.lanes p{font-size:.9rem}.findings a{font-size:.82rem}.annotation{border-left:3px solid var(--orange);background:#f2e9db;padding:14px 20px;margin:24px 0;font-size:.9rem}.lanes article{padding:22px;background:var(--white);border:1px solid var(--line)}.lanes h3{color:var(--teal)}.lanes strong{display:block;line-height:1.4;margin-bottom:14px}.pipeline{display:flex;padding:0;list-style:none;counter-reset:step;margin:28px 0;gap:8px}.pipeline li{flex:1;border-top:1px solid var(--teal);padding:12px 6px;font-size:.8rem}.pipeline li:before{counter-increment:step;content:counter(step) " / ";color:var(--teal);font-weight:700}.table-scroll{overflow-x:auto;margin:24px 0}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.84rem;line-height:1.45;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}caption{text-align:left;margin-bottom:12px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem}th,td{text-align:left;padding:12px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);vertical-align:top}thead th{font-size:.72rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;background:#e7ece5}tbody th{font-weight:500}td{min-width:95px}tbody tr:nth-child(even){background:#ffffff60}.chart-pair,.resource-notes{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:30px}.chart{margin-bottom:10px;min-width:0}.chart svg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;overflow:visible}.chart svg text{font:12px system-ui,sans-serif;fill:var(--muted)}figure{margin:22px 0}figcaption{line-height:1.5}details{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:16px 0;margin:16px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;color:var(--teal);font-weight:600;font-size:.88rem}details[open] summary{margin-bottom:18px}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;background:#e9ede6;padding:18px;font:12px/1.6 ui-monospace,monospace;max-height:540px;overflow:auto}code{font-size:.8em;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.citations dt{font-weight:600;color:var(--teal);margin-top:20px}.citations dd{margin-left:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.empty{border:1px dashed var(--line);padding:25px}.resource-notes article{border-top:2px solid var(--teal);padding-top:20px}.stat{font-family:Georgia,"Times New Roman",serif;font-size:2rem}.stat span{font-size:1.2rem}footer{padding:28px 0 60px;font-size:.75rem;color:var(--muted)}.skip{position:absolute;left:12px;top:-100px;background:var(--white);padding:12px;z-index:2}.skip:focus{top:8px}.legend{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:16px;font-size:.8rem}.legend span:before{content:"";display:inline-block;width:18px;height:3px;background:var(--color);margin-right:6px;vertical-align:middle}.series-summary{font-size:.82rem;color:var(--muted)}@media(max-width:760px){main,.masthead{padding-left:20px;padding-right:20px}.masthead span:last-child{display:none}.hero{padding-top:45px}.findings,.lanes,.chart-pair,.resource-notes{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:10px}nav{gap:12px 20px}section{padding:36px 0}.pipeline{flex-wrap:wrap}.pipeline li{flex:1 1 30%}.findings article{padding:18px 0}.findings h3{font-size:1.8rem}th,td{padding:10px}h1{letter-spacing:-.045em}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){html{scroll-behavior:auto}}@media print{details pre{max-height:none}nav,.skip{display:none}section{break-inside:auto}.findings article,figure{break-inside:avoid}body{background:white}}
.chart{overflow-x:auto}.chart-pair>*{min-width:0}.chart svg{min-width:500px}#contention-charts .chart svg,#outcomes-chart svg{min-width:720px}.worker-toggles{border:0;padding:0;margin:12px 0;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px 20px}.worker-toggles legend{font-size:.8rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:8px}.worker-toggles label{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;font-size:.85rem;cursor:pointer;min-height:32px}.worker-toggles input{accent-color:var(--color);width:18px;height:18px}.worker-toggles input:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--orange);outline-offset:3px}.worker-toggles span{border-bottom:3px solid var(--color)}
</style>{{end}}`
